title: The Three Internationals
subtitle: Moscow, Vienna and London meet in the Reichstag.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1922 and month = 4
max-visits: 1
priority: 2

= The Three Internationals

From 2 to 5 April, the three Internationals meet in the Reichstag building: the Second, of Vandervelde and MacDonald; the Vienna Union of Friedrich Adler, which the workers call the Two-and-a-Half; and our own, represented by Radek, Bukharin and Clara Zetkin. It is the first time since 1914 that they have sat at one table.

The social democrats want guarantees for the Socialist Revolutionaries on trial in Moscow and an end to communist cells in their unions. Radek wants joint demonstrations against the capitalist offensive. A joint commission of nine is proposed, and a day of common marches on 20 April.

The Comintern delegation speaks for the International. But the marches will be ours to organise, and our delegates will be watched by every German worker.

- @real: Treat it as a real beginning, and organise the marches with the SPD.
- @expose: Use the conference to expose the reformist leaders.
- @independent: Demand that the German party speaks for itself at the table.
- @boycott: Stay away from the marches.

@real
subtitle: [? if lock_united_front = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] The Right's hope. Relations with the social democrats improve.
choose-if: lock_united_front < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids marching with the social democrats.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_united_front == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 10;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10;
}
Q.e22_three_int = 1;
Q.spd_relation += 8;
Q.uspd_relation += 8;
Q.worker_support += 4;
Q.unionist_satisfaction += 6;
Q.offensive_satisfaction -= 6;
Q.lean_unionist += 2;
!}

On 20 April a hundred and fifty thousand march in the Lustgarten under red flags of every shade. The commission of nine breaks up within weeks, but the picture of the march stays on many kitchen walls.

@expose
subtitle: The Left's reading. Moscow's line in all but name; the SPD is offended.
view-if: offensive_gone = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.e22_three_int = 2;
Q.spd_relation -= 6;
Q.uspd_relation -= 4;
Q.offensive_satisfaction += 6;
Q.unionist_satisfaction -= 3;
Q.lean_offensive += 2;
Q.militancy += 3;
!}

Our speakers march beside the social democrats and attack them from the platform. The SPD press calls it a trick, and is not wholly wrong.

@independent
subtitle: The Spartacist demand. More independence; Radek is annoyed.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e22_three_int = 3;
Q.independence += 6;
Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction += 6;
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 2;
Q.spd_relation += 2;
!}

[? if luxemburg_alive = 1 : Rosa Luxemburg takes a seat beside Zetkin and speaks for the German workers in a voice the social democrats still remember. ?][? if luxemburg_alive = 0 : Zetkin insists on speaking for the German party and not only for Moscow. ?] Radek complains, but the German delegates are heard.

@boycott
subtitle: Pure hands, empty streets.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e22_three_int = 4;
Q.worker_support -= 3;
Q.spd_relation -= 3;
Q.ultraleft_satisfaction += 4;
Q.unionist_satisfaction -= 5;
!}

Our members watch the marches from the pavement.
